          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "картошка (kartóshka) — \"potatoes\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "картошка (kartóshka) is картофель, \"potato\", with the fond -ошка. картофель came from German Kartoffel, which comes from Italian tartufolo, \"truffle\": the tubers looked like truffles (Vasmer)."
            }
          ]
        },
